+# Canonical validation: 2026-09-25
+
+## Result and authority
+
+- Tested head: `a4888533353238501aa82e355b7c34f3560dadc6`.
+- Command: `node bin/forge.js validate --shards 4`.
+- Started: `2026-09-25T05:31:33.436Z`.
+- Exit: 1 after 1720.253 seconds (28 minutes 40.253 seconds overall).
+- The test phase hit its unchanged 25-minute deadline.
+- Fresh fetch before the run: zero commits behind `origin/master`.
+- Lease: verified under `delivery-reliability-root-20260925`.
+- Receipt verification afterward: `valid: false`, `reason: missing-or-invalid`.
+- Tested head and worktree were unchanged at terminal verification. No push or
+  PR was attempted. No second canonical run was started.
+
+Preflight observed 7.23 GiB free physical memory and eight logical processors.
+An unrelated focused Bun test was present; no Forge full-suite runner was found.
+These are point-in-time observations, not evidence identifying the cause of the
+subsequent timeouts. Increasing available RAM did not suffice to make this run
+complete successfully.
+
+## What actually ran
+
+The captured top-level inventory reports requested/effective budget 4, with 29
+shards across 617 files:
+
+| Group | Files | Shards | Granted concurrency | Terminal evidence |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |
+| Unit | 227 | 4 | 4, deferred | No terminal report |
+| Subprocess | 369 | 4 | 2, cost 2 each | Two terminal reports; two missing |
+| Exclusive | 21 | 21 | 1, cost 2 | No terminal report |
+
+Windows unit work is deliberately deferred behind subprocess work in the
+existing scheduler. Exclusive work follows shared work. A larger budget is not
+permission to overlap these groups or weaken their isolation. The observed
+duration is not a proven scheduler defect or a valid before/after benchmark.
+
+| Completed report | Cases | Failures | Skips | Reported seconds |
+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |
+| `local-full-shard-4.xml` | 1352 | 6 | 0 | 1331.817 |
+| `local-full-shard-5.xml` | 1164 | 0 | 25 | 735.679 |
+
+Only these two terminal reports exist. Missing XML alone does not prove that
+no work started; it leaves that work unverified. These totals must not be
+presented as the result of the full suite. The process tree was checked after exit: none of
+the previously observed runner/worker PIDs or Bun commands naming this report
+directory remained. This is bounded cleanup evidence, not a system-wide orphan
+process audit.
+
+## All observed failures
+
+The six failures in the completed JUnit report were parsed with an XML parser.
+Four additional failures have source locations and error details in the
+captured output of unfinished shards. Wrapped and repeated copies of the same
+failure were deduplicated; raw marker counts are not test counts.
+
+| Source | Case | Observed failure |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `test/check-forge-token.test.js` | Bun-issued proof in the real Node checker | Test timeout, 30.347 s |
+| `test/check-forge-token.test.js:195` | Node-only proof in the Node checker | Child `ETIMEDOUT`, null status, 12.225 s |
+| `test/cli/pr-noun-dispatch.test.js:67` | Shepherd events alias compatibility | Child Bun `ETIMEDOUT`, 56.615 s |
+| `test/cli/pr-noun-dispatch.test.js:66` | Guarded merge alias compatibility | Child Bun `ETIMEDOUT`, 30.131 s |
+| `test/protected-state-surfaces.test.js` | Safe staged edit with reproducible lock | Test timeout, 16.133 s |
+| `test/protected-state-surfaces.test.js` | Reject surface-only environment declaration | Test timeout, 15.103 s |
+| `test/commands/doc-gate-init.test.js` | JSON output equals the scaffold | Test timeout, 30.901 s; no terminal shard XML |
+| `test-env/automation/setup-fixtures.test.js:37` | All 15 fixture directories exist | Existence assertion false |
+| `test-env/automation/setup-fixtures.test.js:85` | Monorepo workspace manifest exists | `pnpm-workspace.yaml` absent |
+| `test-env/automation/setup-fixtures.test.js:92` | Large AGENTS file exists | `ENOENT` for `large-agents-md/AGENTS.md` |
+
+There are ten observed failures: seven timeouts and three missing-fixture
+assertions. Unexecuted and unfinished work remains unknown. No attribution to
+the timeout-evidence change, host load, or a particular shared helper is proven.
+
+## Useful timing evidence
+
+In the completed green shard, setup rerun took 59.53 seconds, the large
+Git-indexed validation fixture 41.86 seconds, setup discovery 27.68 seconds,
+and two status cases 25.20 and 21.74 seconds. Its test-case durations sum to
+664.64 seconds against a shard duration of 735.68 seconds. These are individual
+observations under this workload, not repeatable speedup measurements.
+
+The timeout-evidence implementation was exercised by the real failure: the
+public output retained the resource inventory and subprocess output instead
+of losing it, and completion still failed without a valid receipt. This proves
+that failure path; it does not validate the whole branch.
+
